+## R-011 — Owner-only registration: explicit owner declaration replaces the job-title dropdown (business decision + Director authorization)
+- **ID / date / seat:** R-011 · 29 October 2026 (Asia/Dhaka) · recorded by Claudy (Engineer); business decision is Coach's, implementation authorized by the Director (Tony).
+- **Approving source:** Director dispatch, 29 Oct 2026: "Coach approved owner-only registration and removal of the job-title dropdown. He requires an explicit owner declaration. Tony authorizes this frontend amendment now, before final certification. Preserve the repairs you just completed." … "Email verification establishes control of an inbox. Neither email verification nor payment proves pharmacy ownership or delegated authority. Do not claim otherwise in UI or documentation."
+- **Base:** `qa/ffm-abm-001-subscription-portal` @ `0d43a4c343909467487b327e654e0650b21c9336` (Director commit of REPAIR_001).
+- **Exact decision (frontend / mock contract only):**
+  1. The C02 "Your role" dropdown (Owner / Pharmacist in charge / Manager / Other) and `OwnerDraft.businessRole` are removed.
+  2. A required, initially unchecked checkbox with the exact label "I confirm that I am the pharmacy owner and am registering this account to manage its subscription and pharmacies." is added to C02, with an accessible label, an inline error and an error-summary entry. It is stored as `OwnerDraft.ownerDeclarationAccepted` (must be exactly `true`). It is separate from `ConsentView` (terms, recurring charge, price change).
+  3. The mock service enforces it: `validateOwner` fails without it, so `firstIncomplete`/`isDraftComplete` keep the draft on the owner step and `startCheckout` refuses submission. Drafts persisted before R-011 (public storage version 1) are migrated **without** acceptance; the job title is dropped. Seeded scenarios carry acceptance only through the synthetic `OWNER_JORDAN` fixture, labelled as such.
+  4. "Who will be this store's admin? Me / Someone else" stays. The registering owner keeps account ownership and billing. "Me" = the owner also manages that store. "Someone else" appoints a store admin and does not transfer ownership, billing or permission to buy more stores. One designated admin per store remains the rule.
+  5. Ownership-transfer support copy is kept and clarified: there is no self-service transfer form or working support integration; unresolved details are explicit placeholders (`[SUPPORT EMAIL]`, `[OWNERSHIP TRANSFER PROCESS TBD]`, ownership review process `[TBD]`).
+  6. The declaration is a self-declaration. Neither email nor payment proves ownership or delegated authority; the UI says so and no ownership verification is claimed. Registration, payment, provisioning and access-link delivery remain simulated; no live email verification is introduced.
+- **Unchanged:** database, RLS, stored roles, live auth, Stripe, Mission Control, OwedBook; the real admin/superadmin reviewer gate (R-008/R-009); the real authenticated admin is not relabelled as a provisioned Owner; pharmacy-software choices (separate stakeholder decision); REPAIR_001 behaviour.
